  "title": "Quarterly sales summary",
  "headings": [
    "Overview",
    "Regions",
    "Pipeline",
    "Next quarter"
  ],
  "path": null,
  "text": "# Overview\n\nSales closed the quarter slightly ahead of the target set in January. New business came in below plan, and expansion of existing accounts made up the difference. The average deal took longer to close than last quarter, mostly because larger customers added a security review to their buying process.\n\n# Regions\n\nThe southern region had its best quarter, helped by two large renewals that also added seats. The northern region missed its target after a senior account executive left in the middle of the quarter and their deals were handed to others. The western region was close to plan. The new partner channel produced its first three deals, all small, and the partner team believes the next quarter will show whether the channel can grow.\n\n# Pipeline\n\nThe pipeline for next quarter is healthy in size but young: more than half of its value sits in the first two stages, where deals often stall. The sales team will spend the first month qualifying those deals harder, so the forecast rests on deals that have a budget, a decision maker and a date. Deals that have not moved in sixty days will be closed as lost and reopened only when the customer comes back.\n\n# Next quarter\n\nThe focus is new business. Marketing will run two webinars aimed at the industries where we won last quarter, and the sales team will follow up every attendee within two days. The northern region gets a new account executive in the first week. Pricing stays the same, but the discount any one deal can carry without approval drops, because discounts grew over the last two quarters. The sales leadership will review the forecast every two weeks rather than every month.\n",
